    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d150">

                <pb facs="0454" n="404" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv12/pg404"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 184.01102/208</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Professor A. C. Coolidge to the Commission to
                        Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 140</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-13">March 13, 1919</date>.<lb/>[Received March
                        15.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sirs</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith a
                    series of reports by Captain Nicholas Roosevelt,<anchor n="92" xml:id="d150-f1"
                    /> who has recently made a visit to Bucharest to complete certain studies in
                    connection with Transylvania and the relations between the Hungarians and
                    Roumanians. While not endorsing all of Captain Roosevelt’s opinions, some of
                    which seem to me too sweeping, I beg to call attention to them and to the
                    information contained in the report.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Archibald Cary
                    Coolidge</hi></signed></closer>





                <xi:include href="d150-a1.xml" xpointer="d150-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d150-a2.xml" xpointer="d150-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
